@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.integration"

Feature: Customer To Provisioning License Integration
	Testing to assure that customer license management works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I deactivate the license on provisioning with the name "Activation Key Name" on the account "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                    |
	| Portal Production                 |
	| Commerce Subscription Development |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP OEM                           |
	| DXP Limited                       |
	| DXP Non-Production                |
	| Portal Per User                   |
	| Commerce Subscription Development |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| CSTPROPROCST |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| CSTPROPROCST |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the list of downloaded files "${staticDownloadedListName}"

Scenario: View DXP Production license created in customer on provisoning
	Testing the DXP Production license integration from customer to provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | CSTPROPROCST                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate the account key value for "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"
	And I search the customer projects page using the keyword "Cstpro"
	And I click on the project with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the customer project details page
	And I choose the "DXP" subscription at the product activation tab
	And I click on the generate activation key button on activation keys index
	And I populate the activation key form with the following values
	| Version          | Select       | 7.4                         |
	| Key Type         | Select       | Production                  |
	| Subscription     | Radio Button | Jun 30, 2021 - Mar 30, 2023 |
	And I click on the next button on generate activation key form
	And I populate the activation key form with the following values
	| Environment Name | Input | Activation Key Name        |
	| Description      | Input | Activation Key Description |
	| Host Name        | Input | localhost                  |
	| IP Address       | Input | 123.45.67.89               |
	| MAC Address      | Input | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F          |
	And I click on the generate button on the generate activation key form
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "Activation Key Name"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Activation Key Name" and the following values
	| Name          | Activation Key Name            |
	| Description   | Activation Key Description     |
	| Account       | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | DXP Production                 |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                         |
	| Complimentary | false                          |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Activation Key Name" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.4                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Activation Key Description    | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Test Test                     | |

Scenario: View Portal Production license on customer
	Testing the Portal Production license integration from koroneiki to customer

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | CSTPROPROCST                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate the account key value for "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"
	And I search the customer projects page using the keyword "Cstpro"
	And I click on the project with the name "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the customer project details page
	And I choose the "DXP" subscription at the product activation tab
	And I click on the generate activation key button on activation keys index
	And I populate the activation key form with the following values
	| Version          | Select       | 6.1 GA1                     |
	| Key Type         | Select       | Production                  |
	| Subscription     | Radio Button | Oct 30, 2022 - Oct 30, 2023 |
	And I click on the next button on generate activation key form
	And I populate the activation key form with the following values
	| Environment Name | Input  | Activation Key Name        |
	| Description      | Input  | Activation Key Description |
	| Host Name        | Input  | localhost                  |
	| IP Address       | Input  | 123.45.67.89               |
	| MAC Address      | Input  | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F          |
	And I click on the generate button on the generate activation key form
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" and the following values
	| Name          | Activation Key Name            |
	| Description   | Activation Key Description     |
	| Account       | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | Portal Production              |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                         |
	| Complimentary | false                          |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Cstpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | Portal Production             | |
	| Version       | 6.1 GA1                       | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Cstpro - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Activation Key Description    | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Test Test                     | |

Scenario: View Commerce Development license on customer
	Testing the Commerce Development license integration from koroneiki to customer

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
